Installation Process
1. Repository Database Setup
Installed DBA Dash repository database on the designated SQL Server instance.
Configured database settings and permissions.
Validated connectivity and service account access.
2. DBA Dash Agent Deployment
Installed DBA Dash service on target monitoring server.
Connected agents to the central repository.
Configured secure communication between monitored servers and repository database.
3. Monitoring Configuration

Configured monitoring for:

SQL Server availability
CPU utilization
Memory consumption
Disk space usage
Database growth
Backup status
Job execution status
Wait statistics
Blocking and deadlocks
4. Security Configuration
Assigned least-privilege SQL permissions.
Configured service accounts.
Validated repository and monitored instance access.
Validation and Testing
Verified successful data collection from monitored SQL instances.
Confirmed dashboard visibility and report generation.
Tested alerting and notification functionality.
Validated performance metrics collection and historical data retention.
Outcome

The DBA Dash implementation provides a centralized view of SQL Server health and performance across the MGE environment, enabling proactive monitoring, faster issue resolution, and improved operational visibility for database administration teams.

